.TH SHENG-BOOT-SLOT 8 "August 2026" "mkinitcpio-bootflash" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sheng-boot-slot \- safely install one Xiaomi sheng A/B boot slot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sheng-boot-slot status
.br
.B sheng-boot-slot install --slot
.IR a | b
.RB [ --image " " FILE ]
.RB [ --backup-dir " " DIR ]
.RB [ --force-active ]
.br
.B sheng-boot-slot restore --slot
.IR a | b
.B --backup
.I FILE
.RB [ --force-active ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sheng-boot-slot
never selects both slots and never writes a slot implicitly.  Installation
backs up the complete selected partition before writing, verifies that backup,
then verifies the written image prefix.  Restoration requires a complete backup
whose size exactly matches the selected partition.
.PP
The active slot is discovered from Android boot arguments and the vbmeta
PARTUUID.  It is refused by default.  If discovery is impossible, writes are
also refused by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --slot a|b
Select exactly one target slot.
.TP
.BI --image " FILE"
Image to install.  The default is /boot/boot.img.
.TP
.BI --backup-dir " DIR"
Directory for full-partition backups.  The default is
/var/lib/sheng-boot-slot.
.TP
.BI --backup " FILE"
Full-partition backup to restore.
.TP
.B --force-active
Permit a write when the selected slot is active or active-slot discovery
failed.  This option removes an important recovery safeguard.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/disk/by-partlabel/boot_a
.TP
.I /dev/disk/by-partlabel/boot_b
.TP
.I /var/lib/sheng-boot-slot
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sheng-boot-slot status
sudo sheng-boot-slot install --slot a --image /boot/boot.img
sudo sheng-boot-slot restore --slot a --backup /var/lib/sheng-boot-slot/boot_a-TIMESTAMP.img
.fi
